# Riverchurn Monument: "{1}, {T}: Any number of target players each mill two cards" and "Exhaust - {2}{U}{U}, {T}: Any
# number of target players each mill cards equal to the number of cards in their graveyard. (Activate each exhaust
# ability only once.)" On turn 3 Bot1 targets both players: each mills their top two, the second card above the first
# (CR 701.17). On turn 4 Bot2 bolts Bot1, so Bot2's graveyard holds three cards to Bot1's two. On turn 5 the exhaust
# targets both: Bot1 mills two and Bot2 three, each by their own graveyard as it resolves. On turn 7 the exhaust is
# not offered again, with its mana there, while the first ability still is (the positive control), at Bot2 alone.

